## Decisions Made
- Adapted (not verbatim) versions of mattpocock skills to preserve project voice + avoid file-level MIT attribution overhead in SKILL.md
- Single root CONTEXT.md only, no multi-context (CONTEXT-MAP.md) support — YAGNI
- All 4 new skills + tdd boost shipped in a single PR (not phased)
- Slash commands added for grill + zoom-out only (not for vocabulary or architecture); the latter rely on auto-trigger
- Attribution lives in README + CHANGELOG, not in SKILL.md headers
- Deferred evals/ and scripts/ infrastructure to keep skill-set internally consistent (no existing skill ships those)
- Applied skill-creator audit fixes: pushy descriptions, voodoo-constant justification, MUST/exactly framing softened with why-prefixed reasoning

## Problems Encountered
- Initial verbatim-copy request conflicted with prior clean-SKILL.md decision — resolved by clarifying it was feature parity, not text reuse
- Two rounds of audit (creating-skills, then skill-creator) surfaced different gap classes — resolved by triaging via autofixing-and-escalating: OBVIOUS auto-applied, AMBIGUOUS user-approved, low-value/scope-creep deferred
- Direct git commit blocked by knowledge-distillery pre-commit hook — resolved by switching to memento-commit workflow

## Constraints Identified
- skill-set has no existing evals/ or scripts/ infrastructure; adding to only the 4 new skills would create inconsistency the project does not want
- mattpocock content is MIT but verbatim reproduction at scale conflicts with the project's adaptation/voice convention; per-file attribution would be the only license-clean path for verbatim reuse
- Pre-commit hook in this repo mandates memento-commit; direct git commit fails fast

## Open Questions
- Whether to retroactively add evals/ across all skill-set skills as a separate project (deferred)
- Whether to add bundled scripts (LSP wrappers, e.g.) for the repeated-work cases skill-creator flagged (deferred)

## Context
Session goal: extend skill-set with patterns from mattpocock/skills. Final delivery includes 4 new skills (grilling-plans, building-shared-vocabulary, zooming-out-on-code, improving-architecture), a Horizontal Slicing anti-pattern addition to developing-test-first, two slash commands, and a 1.11.1 to 1.12.0 version bump. Three review rounds tightened triggers, voodoo constants, and imperative framing while keeping all SKILL.md files under the 200-line target.

